<BaseLayout title="About this reference">
  <h1>About this reference</h1>
  <p>This site is an independent, owner-focused reference for the North American 2021-model-year, third-generation Volvo S60 range. Its purpose is to make operating information, system explanations, maintenance planning, component identification and repair research easier to navigate than scattered notes, forum posts and generic parts listings.</p>
  <h2>Vehicle coverage</h2>
  <p>The reference covers T5, T6, T8 Recharge and Polestar Engineered variants where the information is available. It distinguishes front-wheel drive, mechanical all-wheel drive and T8 electric-rear-axle layouts. Some owner observations relate to a 2021 S60 T5 Inscription AWD in Denim Blue; that example is not the assumed configuration for every page.</p>
  <h2>How to use it</h2>
  <p>Use the navigation to browse by vehicle system or task, the visual parts atlas to jump between component areas, and site search to find terms across the reference. Maintenance pages separate factory-listed operations from conditional or owner-planning recommendations. Repair pages should identify configuration, preparation, tools, a safe overview, inspection checks and the source required for the full procedure.</p>
  <h2>How information is labeled</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Volvo owner information:</strong> official operating guidance and illustrations for the specified model year/market.</li>
    <li><strong>Factory service information:</strong> required for VIN-specific repair procedures, torque values, wiring, programming, fluid-level procedures and diagnostic tests.</li>
    <li><strong>Independent estimates:</strong> secondary cost references or planning allowances, clearly identified as estimates rather than Volvo quotes.</li>
    <li><strong>Representative images:</strong> photographs or diagrams that illustrate a component or vehicle family, with model-year and fitment limitations stated.</li>
    <li><strong>Owner observations:</strong> practical notes that are not presented as factory specifications.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Accuracy and safety</h2>
  <p>Engine, transmission, drivetrain, brakes, suspension, electrical systems, market equipment and production details can differ. Verify parts and specifications using the VIN and installed component markings. Never infer fitment from a trim badge or a photograph alone. T8 high-voltage work requires appropriately trained technicians and Volvo-approved equipment and procedures.</p>
  <p>Where reliable public information is incomplete, the page should say so rather than invent a value or procedure. This site is not a substitute for the owner's manual, factory workshop information, professional diagnosis, or safe repair practices, and it is not affiliated with Volvo Cars.</p>
  <p>See <a href="../../resources/source-notes/">Source notes and accuracy</a> for source hierarchy and model-year boundaries.</p>
</BaseLayout>
